<BaseLayout title="About Wanda" description="Wanda's research in quantum control, neutral-atom quantum computing, Rydberg interactions, and numerical optimization.">
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A NOTE FROM THE AUTHOR</p><h1>About</h1><p>The research I do, and the ideas I work through along the way.</p></header>
  <article class="about-copy">
    <p class="about-lead">Hello, I'm Wanda.</p>
    <p>I work on quantum control and neutral-atom quantum computing, using theoretical models and numerical simulations to study how atomic interactions can be used to perform quantum operations. My research focuses on Rydberg interactions, entangling gates, and pulse design, including schemes that use different atomic species.</p>
    <p>My computational work includes LLM-guided control design, automated pulse optimization, and simulation-based checks of gate performance, with attention to noise and control imperfections. I also explore measurement-free quantum error correction and how the control of atomic systems can help protect quantum information.</p>

    <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="about-site-heading">
      <h2 id="about-site-heading">A notebook and a collection of work</h2>
      <p><a href="/notes/">Research Notes</a> is my working notebook: explanations of physical ideas, notes on papers, calculations, and methods I am exploring. Some entries start from the basics; others work through technical details.</p>
      <p><a href="/work/">Selected Work</a> brings together papers, research projects, and computational tools from my work. It is a place to see the questions behind a project, what the work contributes, and where to find the paper or code.</p>
      <p>Across both, I aim to make the physical reasoning clear: what a method does, why it works, and where its assumptions matter.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="interests-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH &amp; INTERESTS</p>
      <h2 id="interests-heading">What I work on and explore</h2>
      <div class="topic-grid about-interests">
        {interests.map((item, index) => <div class="topic-item"><span>0{index + 1}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><small>{item.description}</small></div>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="about-disclaimer">The views and explanations here are my own and are not official statements from any institution or employer. Research details are shared with care for publication status and collaboration agreements.</p>
    <div class="about-signoff">Wanda<br/><span>Neutral atoms · Quantum control · Research notes</span></div>
    <p class="about-contact">Find me on <a href="https://github.com/wanda0929" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>.</p>
  </article>
